# Component Standards

- Functional components only, TypeScript, explicit prop interfaces (`{ComponentName}Props`).
- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when the component needs state,
  effects, browser APIs, or event handlers. Push `"use client"` as far down the tree as
  possible — a page can be a Server Component even if one child chart is client-rendered.
- One component per file. Co-locate a component's Storybook/test file next to it
  (`RecommendationCard.tsx`, `RecommendationCard.test.tsx`).
- Every list/table component accepts `isLoading` and `isEmpty` states explicitly and
  renders `components/feedback/LoadingSkeletons.tsx` / `EmptyState.tsx` — never a bare
  spinner or a silently blank div.
- Dashboard widgets (`KpiTile`, chart wrappers) must accept a `scope` prop
  (`company | department | team | employee`) rather than being hardcoded to one role's
  dashboard — this is what lets `/analytics` and `/roi` stay single routes (see
  `000-project-context.mdc` principle 5).
- No inline business logic in JSX. Compute derived values in the hook, pass primitives/
  formatted strings into the component.
